# New-line braces (Allman)

Put the opening `{` on the next line, at the same indent as the statement. Do not use K&R (`if (x) {`).

Applies to functions, methods, lambdas, `if` / `else` / `for` / `while` / `switch` / `do`, classes, structs, enums, and namespaces.

Keep `Foo{1, 2}` and `std::vector<int>{}` braced-init on one line. Do not write `if (x) stmt;` — always use braces.

```cpp
// BAD
void tick(int n) {
    if (n > 0) {
        run();
    } else {
        stop();
    }
}

// GOOD
void tick(int n)
{
    if (n > 0)
    {
        run();
    }
    else
    {
        stop();
    }
}
```
